<section class="frame recommendation-panel"><div><span class="micro">My recommendation</span><h2>A’s reason to care.<br />B’s proof.<br />C’s foundation.</h2></div><div><p><strong>Use equipment first as the homepage angle.</strong> Your neighbours’ reality gives it substance: they bought what they could afford over time and want it to work together.</p><p>Follow that with a useful site view, then explain the local architecture and open stack. Give the products their own pages once the visitor understands why they need the system.</p><a class="text-action" href="/next/research/">Read the research & business opportunities ↗</a></div></section>
<section class="open-band"><div class="frame"><span class="micro">Beyond the homepage / Working in this draft</span><div class="research-grid" style="margin-top:30px"><article><span class="micro">A way to find us</span><h3>Equipment directory</h3><p>Search the actual research catalogue, filter evidence and carry a model into a site enquiry.</p><a href="/next/equipment/">Find your equipment ↗</a></article><article><span class="micro">A way to understand it</span><h3>Sample site</h3><p>Explore a cottage overview and see how the app treats readings when a connection drops.</p><a href="/next/sample-site/">Explore the sample ↗</a></article><article><span class="micro">A way to go deeper</span><h3>A complete site</h3><p>Dedicated products, cottage and field applications, open-stack status and a practical setup enquiry.</p><a href="/next/system/">Explore the system ↗</a></article></div></div></section>
<section class="frame section-pad"><div class="two-column"><div><span class="micro">Review notes</span><h2>Claims with<br />something behind them.</h2></div><div><p style="font-size:18px">The catalogue contains {counts.entries.toLocaleString('en')} research entries, including passive equipment, series and repeats. It is not a count of validated integrations. The full open stack is the intended direction; the draft makes the current source and licence status visible.</p><p style="margin-top:20px">These are design and product concepts in development. Controller imagery comes from the existing CAD model, with earlier enclosure artwork. App data is illustrative.</p><div class="actions"><a class="text-action" href="/next/research/">Sources & claim audit ↗</a><a class="text-action" href="/round-1/">Compare with round 01 ↗</a></div></div></div></section>
